---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Contact | salarynegotiationcalc.com';
const description = 'Contact the salarynegotiationcalc.com editorial team with corrections, feedback, or questions about salary negotiation content.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Contact salarynegotiationcalc.com</h1>
  <p>The best way to reach us is by email at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We read every message and respond to substantive corrections and editorial feedback within five business days.</p>

  <h2>What We Can Help With</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Factual corrections:</strong> If you have identified an incorrect industry multiplier, a location premium inconsistent with current BLS data, or a negotiation claim unsupported by published research, share the specific claim, the page URL, and your source.</li>
    <li><strong>Methodology questions:</strong> The <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> documents all calculator assumptions. For follow-up questions, email us.</li>
    <li><strong>Content suggestions:</strong> If a negotiation scenario, industry-specific consideration, or practical topic is missing from the guides or FAQ, suggestions are welcome.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Cannot Help With</h2>
  <p>We cannot provide personalized career advice or case-specific negotiation guidance. We do not respond to questions like "Should I accept this offer?", "How much should I ask for at [specific company]?", or "Is this a good salary for my situation?" For personalized guidance, consider working with a career coach or compensation consultant.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>salarynegotiationcalc.com is monetized exclusively through Google AdSense display advertising. We do not accept sponsored content, paid placements, or advertising arrangements with employers, recruiters, or career platforms.</p>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a> or see the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
